# Bloodline Design System Rules

## Brand Identity

The UI must feel:

- aggressive
- premium
- cinematic
- tactical
- energetic
- high-trust

Avoid:
- soft luxury aesthetics
- playful startup styling
- generic SaaS visuals
- futuristic cyberpunk overload
- editorial minimal fashion layouts

---

## Typography Rules

### Heading Font

Use:

```txt
Barlow Condensed
```

### Body Font

Use:

```txt
Plus Jakarta Sans
```

---

## Heading Behavior

All major headings should default to:

- uppercase
- tight tracking
- aggressive hierarchy
- condensed structure
- bold weight

Headings are part of the brand identity.

Avoid:
- lowercase hero headings
- decorative typography
- loose tracking
- soft typography rhythm

---

## Color Rules

Primary colors:

```txt
Background: #0B0B0D
Accent: #C6FF3B
```

Do not introduce random brand colors.

---

## Token Rules

Use semantic tokens only.

Preferred:

```tsx
className="bg-background text-foreground"
className="text-accent border-border"
```

Avoid arbitrary values:

```tsx
className="bg-[#0B0B0D]"
className="text-[#C6FF3B]"
className="rounded-[17px]"
```

Only use arbitrary values when absolutely necessary.

---

## Surface Rules

Use layered dark surfaces.

Approved hierarchy:

- background
- surface
- surface-elevated
- surface-strong

Avoid:
- flat endless black sections
- excessive glassmorphism
- random gradients
- bright surfaces

---

## Layout Rules

Layouts should feel:

- structured
- cinematic
- proof-heavy
- breathable
- tactical

Avoid:
- chaotic asymmetry
- cluttered layouts
- excessive whitespace minimalism
- Pinterest-style randomness

---

## Spacing Rules

Use:
- strong vertical rhythm
- large cinematic section spacing
- controlled density

Avoid:
- cramped UI
- tiny spacing
- oversized empty luxury spacing

---

## Border Rules

Borders should be:
- subtle
- tactical
- low-opacity

Use borders for:
- structure
- separation
- rhythm

Avoid:
- heavy card outlines
- excessive divider clutter

---

## Radius Rules

Use restrained radius values.

The UI should feel:
- sharp
- tactical
- structured

Avoid:
- oversized pill radius
- overly soft SaaS corners

---

## Shadow Rules

Use shadows minimally.

Prefer:
- contrast
- layering
- subtle elevation

Avoid:
- heavy blurred glow systems
- floating card shadows
- dramatic neumorphism

---

## Glow Rules

Accent glow usage should remain restrained.

Allowed:
- CTA hover glow
- active states
- tactical highlights

Avoid:
- constant neon glow
- cyberpunk lighting effects

---

## CTA Rules

Primary CTA tone should feel:

- confident
- premium
- direct
- action-oriented

Primary CTA platform:

```txt
WhatsApp
```

Avoid:
- generic SaaS CTA wording
- corporate marketing language
- weak CTA hierarchy

---

## Card Rules

Cards should feel:

- premium
- dark
- tactical
- structured

Avoid:
- soft startup cards
- excessive gradients
- playful UI styling

---

## Image Rules

Tattoo imagery is proof content.

Images should feel:

- cinematic
- immersive
- sharp
- high contrast
- authentic

Avoid:
- stock-photo treatment
- washed-out imagery
- decorative filler media

---

## Gallery Rules

Gallery systems should feel:

```txt
Curated craftsmanship showcase
```

NOT:
```txt
random media dump
```

Use:
- strong crops
- aggressive visual hierarchy
- tactical overlays
- subtle hover depth

---

## Review UI Rules

Reviews should feel:

- authentic
- premium
- trust-heavy

Avoid:
- SaaS testimonial layouts
- fake case study styling
- playful quote blocks

---

## Section Rhythm Rules

Pages should follow:

```txt
Attention
→ Trust
→ Proof
→ Depth
→ Conversion
```

Avoid:
- filler sections
- random decorative blocks
- repetitive layout patterns

---

## Motion Rules

Motion should feel:

- fast
- cinematic
- sharp
- controlled

Allowed:
- fade reveals
- stagger reveals
- subtle scale
- hover zoom

Forbidden:
- bounce
- spin
- exaggerated parallax
- gimmicky animation

---

## Accessibility Rules

Maintain:
- semantic hierarchy
- readable contrast
- visible focus states
- reduced motion support

Luxury styling must never reduce usability.

---

## Mobile Rules

Mobile UI should feel:

- dense but readable
- tactical
- premium

Prioritize:
- strong typography
- optimized spacing
- sticky CTA usability
- fast media loading

Avoid:
- oversized mobile spacing
- tiny typography
- overloaded mobile animation

---

## Reuse Rules

Prefer:
- reusable variants
- reusable sections
- reusable layout systems

Avoid:
- one-off styling
- duplicated section patterns
- inconsistent spacing systems

---

## Forbidden Visual Patterns

Never introduce:

- pastel aesthetics
- playful gradients
- glassmorphism overload
- futuristic UI clutter
- oversized rounded pills
- random typography systems
- editorial fashion minimalism
- bright white layouts

---

## Final Principle

Every visual decision should reinforce:

- trust
- craftsmanship
- authority
- energy
- premium positioning
- conversion confidence

If a visual decision weakens the Bloodline identity, do not implement it.